# Source retrieval and legal validation

## Select the authority, not a preferred database

| Question | Initial authoritative route |
|---|---|
| Italian legislation and its versions | [Normattiva](https://www.normattiva.it/), then the promulgated and amending texts in [Gazzetta Ufficiale](https://www.gazzettaufficiale.it/) |
| Regional rules, grants and individual measures | The issuing authority, its official bulletin and the actual application portal; obtain the version and annexes governing the application |
| Administrative judgments and opinions | [Giustizia Amministrativa](https://www.giustizia-amministrativa.it/), decision/opinion search and full text |
| Constitutional judgments | [Corte costituzionale](https://www.cortecostituzionale.it/) |
| Ordinary-court precedent | [Corte di cassazione](https://www.cortedicassazione.it/) and the issuing court's published judgments; identify coverage gaps actually encountered |
| EU law and judgments | [EUR-Lex](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/) and [Curia](https://curia.europa.eu/) |
| Convention rights | [HUDOC](https://hudoc.echr.coe.int/) |
| Agency practice, tax, privacy or regulated sectors | The competent authority's original act; distinguish guidance from binding law |

These are routing links, not evidence that a particular proposition has been checked. Open the actual source. Do not cite a homepage or a search snippet for a specific rule. A document hosted by a public body may still be a third party's manual; inspect its author and purpose.

## Resolve time and conflicting copies

Record the provision, version date, relevant event date and consultation date. When an official cached page conflicts with a later amendment, obtain the amending law and conversion/transitional provisions. Determine which text governs the event or procedural step. Merely opening an official URL does not establish currency, and the newest text does not necessarily govern old facts.

Treat court guides as guidance on process, not substitutes for a statute. Check a guide's date and any later reform. A superseded heading may coexist with a still-valid rule. Check both rather than accepting or rejecting the entire guide at once.

Read the actual funding call and attached forms. Keep the authority's instructions, the governing legislation, and any challenge to the legality of a call clause distinct. The phrase “public call” does not establish that procurement legislation applies.

## Validate judgments

Record court, section where supplied, decision/opinion type, date, number and direct link. Inspect facts, issue decided, ratio and disposition. Do not convert a party's submission quoted in a judgment into the court's holding. Distinguish a merits judgment from interim relief and an advisory opinion.

An official summary is citable as an official summary, with that limit. For a decisive litigation argument, obtain the underlying decision if possible. If it cannot be retrieved, explain how that limits the argument rather than implying a full-text check occurred. Seek later or adverse treatment when it could change the conclusion; no search guarantees an exhaustive citator result.

Secondary commentary can locate authorities and illuminate competing interpretations. Cite it as commentary, not as the decision itself. Use lawful accessible materials; do not assume all proprietary services prohibit all authorized use or that they are available in this environment.

## Minimal audit trail

For a substantial memo or proposed filing keep a small claim-to-source table: proposition, source/passage, temporal scope, and application or unresolved issue. Reuse it for the user's answer and draft. Quote accurately and sparingly; summarize the rest. Never reconstruct a case number, quotation, article subdivision or URL from a plausible pattern and report it as verified.
